Coach lesson list on Dashboard (delayed checkIn / no show)
*Updated 2026-10-12 to match the Harbor design. The design is the source of truth.*

shows a list of students who had lessons by date range. Makes the coach select a date range before the list appears. 

The page will display the student information, if the lesson was attended (ie checked in) or no showed

The coach will need the following abilities:
to Change the status of a student's lesson to either attended or no showed.

*Design (lessons-empty.html, lessons.html):*
  From and To dates. Nothing is listed until both are set; an end date before the start shows an error.
  Only lessons that have already happened are listed: skater, day, time, length, family, and an Attended / No-show switch.
  A lesson with no attendance is flagged "Not recorded", with a banner explaining the rinkside app may still be holding
  a check-in that hasn't been sent, or nobody recorded it.
  The heading gives the count attended, no-show and not recorded.
  This is where mistakes made at the rink are fixed; the rinkside app can't change a recorded lesson.
  Switching a lesson to No-show doesn't change its price; it stays unpaid until marked paid or waived on Payments.
  *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 15):* in a shared lesson each skater has their own row and their own attendance.

Why corrections are on the website:
  Settled by the owner, 2026-08-30: the coach can correct or undo a recorded outcome, from the coach dashboard on the
  website, not from the rinkside app. The lesson list shows students who had lessons in a required date range with
  their attended / no-show state, and the coach can change a lesson's status to either value.
  Correction is website-only by design. The phone is used with gloves on, at a rink, between lessons. It is where
  mis-taps happen and the worst place to offer an overwrite next to the button that caused one. The dashboard has a
  date range, full context and no hurry.
  *Ruled by the owner 2026-11-09.* The rinkside page has no Undo; Coach App and the design now match.
  *(from ADR-014 §8 and Open, moved 2026-11-08)*

When older lessons are archived:
  A coach who looks for a two-year-old lesson finds nothing, and nothing says why.
  *Settled 2026-10-12 by the owner:* history screens say lessons settled more than *N* months ago are archived and can
  be requested, with *N* read from the retention setting. A warning before archiving is Phase 2.
  The financial page's summary export (MVP, decided 2026-10-12) lets a coach keep their yearly totals before records
  age out (see Coach Financial Page.md).
  ADR-017 says "history screens", so this applies to the family's history too (see C_Client My Bookings.md, "Older lessons").
  *(from ADR-017 Status amendment 2026-10-12 and Open, moved 2026-11-08)*
